{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>For all the peoples.</b> To illuminate for them, even for ordinary people — and lowly is the one who bows to a thing that was created for his use. Another interpretation: <b>which He allotted to all the peoples</b> — that their fear of them be upon them, for He does not concern Himself with them. But <b>you He took to be for Him as a nation of inheritance</b> — so how could you bow to them? Therefore you have no authority to serve any other fear (object of awe) but Him."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:51:38.872206541Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}